ontent/pkg/FR-1961-02-21/pdf/FR-1961-02-21.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: c989a6616bc2b5689ef17a8383fc5abd688db3f15b180ca166ccac69f2812768\nLocation: 26 FR 1463, PDF pages 3-3 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 3 of 24 ===\nPresidential Documents\nTitle 3— THE PRESIDENT\nExecutive O rder 10919\nCREATING AN EM ERGEN CY BOARD  \nTO  INVESTIGATE A  DISPUTE BE­\nTWEEN THE PAN AMERICAN  \nWORLD AIRW AYS, INC., AND CER­\nTAIN OF ITS EMPLOYEES\nWHEREAS a dispute exists between \nthe Pan American World Airways, Inc., \na carrier, and certain of its employees \nrepresented by the Plight Engineers’  In ­\nternational Association, PAA Chapter, a \nlabor organization; and \nWHEREAS this dispute has not here­\ntofore been adjusted under the provisions \nof the Railway Labor Act, as amended; \nand ____\nWHEREAS this dispute, in the judg­\nment of the National Mediation Board, \nthreatens substantially to interrupt in­\nterstate nnrtimfirp.fi to a degree such as to \ndeprive the country of essential trans­\nportation service:\nNOW, THEREFORE, by virtue of the \nauthority vested in  me by section 10 O f \nthe Railway Labor Act, as amended (45 \nU.S.C. 160) , 3 hereby create a board of \nthree members, to be appointed by me, to \ninvestigate this disput","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10919.txt","sha256":"68d4cfc3d168f13f20920015df2050c96f055210549b645c55365707f8f68e4d","source":{"line":977,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"2896c76fa26401b223c7b912ecdfe0bc17debe6440e97d41878da11dfd7587c9"}}]}
